{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1391568-princes-of-pak-kret","id":1391568,"title":"Princes of Pak Kret","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-25T17:10:38-07:00","id":1391568,"title":"Princes of Pak Kret","content":"So lately I caught up with the Strange Predators &amp; Stranger Prey thread, and I read Chris Allen's writeup for the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1237714-strange-predators-and-stranger-prey?p=1276613#post1276613\">Red Prince</a>. While the Red Prince is cool all by itself, it did brought some thoughts about an expanded Pak Kret setting, which felt to me as some form of a dark mirror for Tokyo. Where Tokyo presented a setting of all different supernatural creatures with interacting societies all bound by the scheming Hototogisu and the Envoys to the Others which serve the local Freehold, Pak Kret seems to be a place of fear and horror, where all supernaturals are being pushed to the bring under the horrible occupation of the Broken Majesty and its Princes- Hive Claimed monstrosities who were once the protagonists of the main gamelines. Of those, we have the Red Prince fully detailed, and the Black and White Princes being mentioned as a part of the &quot;court&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, while nothing in the writeup states the number of the Princes or state that every &quot;gameline protagonist&quot; has a representative Prince, I do think it could be a cool thought experiment to see what kind of horrors could the Broken Majesty produce out of the different splats of the world, especially as I am a sucker for colour coded antagonists, and beside it would give us the opportunity to re-imagine each of the monsters of the world as a corrupted, Hive Claimed version of themselves (if not an whole corrupted template), which should have some value on its own right.<br /> <br /> Anyway, as I said earlier, the known Princes are the Red Prince of twisted vampires, the Black Prince of former werewolves and the White Prince of soulless mages. That leaves Promethean, Changeling, Hunter, Geist, Mummy, Demon, Beast and Deviant. A promethean Prince, while cool, could feel a bit like a stretch, considering how rare they are meant to be and how fractured their society is. However, an <i>alchemist</i> would make a great candidate to become a Prince, I believe, and an Hive Claimed alchemist would indeed be a terrifying antagonist to the Created. As for a colour- the Purple Prince feels natural because of the cover, but I think that for an alchemist, the Golden Prince would make a much more fitting title.<br /> <br /> Changeling, on the other hand, would be an easy one. I could definitely see a changeling who would recognize the Unbroken Majesty as the greatest power in the Freehold, and offer a Bargain to it an an attempt to forge a Court (see Oak, Ash and Thorn). That would work, of course, and would still blow up in the unfortunate changeling's face, creating the Green Prince. I assume that the Green Prince may even focus most of their attention in occupying the Hedge, creating twisted hobgoblins in their service of the King.<br /> <br /> Having an hunter as a Prince, however, would make little to no sense. I mean, hunters are human, after all, and would be no different than the usual, giant Hive Claimed. Maybe a slasher? Now, that could be terrifying, especially when combined with 2e's slasher epidemic. Having such Grey Prince could work- but another candidate would a be an Otodo/Lucifuge, who do have some latent supernatural abilities. On the other hand, Tokyo does have two different Envoys- one for hunters, and one for the Otodo. Does Pak Kret needs two such Princes? Or a single, Ashen Prince would cover that niche good enough?<br /> <br /> I think that the Sin Eaters are normally immune to being Claimed (they are already occupied, after all), but I guess that one of the things that idigam do is not playing by the rules. Perhaps instead of creating a spirit Hive Claimed, the poor Bound would become a ghost Hive Claimed, having the Broken Majesty weaving countless desperate voices into a cacophony of madness. I wonder what motivation would that Prince have for their own creation- perhaps they would try to create their own &quot;Dead Dominion&quot; in the world of the living. Perhaps they would take the battle to the Underworld, and would try to take over it in the name of the King. Oh, the Reapers would probably be pissed! As for colour- Gold and Black are already taken.. so maybe Purple for the Bound? Or maybe Blue/Azure, like rivers and tears? On the other hand, the Silver Prince would be an awesome reference to Exalted. Sure, let's go with that.<br /> <br /> Again, I don't think that the Arisen can be normally Claimed, and while the Broken Majesty may be powerful and many idigam can have god like states, we are talking about messing with the Judges, which sounds to me like a bad, bad idea. Same for the Shuankhsen- Ammut is a very jealous entity, and she doesn't like to share. An Immortal, on the other hand, could work- or maybe even am Inheritor, or a Sadikh, someone who grows envious of their god kings, and want to be like them, and the King does the best he can in order to recreate them in that image. Perhaps it would even add some amkhata to the mix, just for fun. At any case, I think I would call that Prince the Yellow Prince- or maybe, the &quot;Prince in Yellow&quot; :P<br /> <br /> Now, let's see how well the idigam can play with being a God Machine! A demon searches after hell, and stumbles upon the greatest demon around. I could see the Hive Claiming being resulted with a fractal nature of that Prince, existing in a number of covers in the same time instead of growing big and bloated with power. They would literally be an Hive, and may even take over other demons and angels &quot;Agent Smith style&quot; to propagate themselves, turning into an horrible virus. Heck, add some Contagion for it just for laughs. While most Princes have their names after colours, the Unseen Prince does makes a fitting name for such entity.<br /> <br /> Beasts are creatures of fear, and god knows that the Majesty is probably the Apex of this setting (well, either it or the magath, but we are talking about the idigam right now). Perhaps a Beast searches after Kinship with the idigam, seeing it as their family- only to become twisted and corrupted by it? On the other hand, as a Beast, they may be more equipped with becoming an Hive, as their Lair would contain all of those different, twisted spirits inside their soul? Heck, maybe the idigam would throw a number of Horrors together into the Lair of the Beast, combining them together like a twisted chimera? Again, we are reaching the time to colour code our villain, and I think that this time, we found our Purple Prince... unless Bronze fits better?<br /> <br /> Finally, we have the Deviants- we could have it that their Prince would go rogue, but that would be too much tongue in the cheek, if you ask me. Perhaps they are the result of a Deviant created by a conspiracy which aimed to harness the Majesty's power? A Devoted who sacrificed themselves to the King in the name of their loyalty? A Renegade who brokered with the idigam for the destruction of his conspiracy, or perhaps in a desperate attempt to stabilize their Divergence? There are many possibilities, honestly. The Vermilion Prince (as it is a much fancier name than the Orange Prince, while vermilion is still technically an hue of orange, even if more of red) could be a very interesting character indeed- some kind of a &quot;messiah&quot; for the Deviants who seek for stability, only to find horror.<br /> <br /> So, let's sum it up, shall we?<br /> <br /> Vampire- Red Prince<br /> Werewolf- Black Prince<br /> Mage- White Prince<br /> Promethean/Alchemist- Golden Prince<br /> Changeling- Green Prince<br /> Lucifuge/Slasher- Ashen Prince<br /> Sin Eater- Silver Prince<br /> Mummy/Immortal- Yellow Prince/ Prince in Yellow<br /> Demon- Unseen Prince/ Prince Invisible<br /> Beast- Purple/ Brazen Prince<br /> Deviant- Vermilion/ Orange Prince<br /> <br /> Of course, that leaves us without a Brown, Blue and possibly Purple Prince (Purple is important enough to find a Prince for even without a gameline, while copper/ bronze/ brass not so much). That would take some thought about filling those niches, while not making it feel forced.<br /> <br /> Anyway, that's what I have for now- what do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T07:46:13-07:00","id":1391678,"title":"","content":"I don't really expect a Hive-Claimed Deviant to amount to much but a catastrophic surge of Instability, and the general lack of any social structure among the Remade makes the idea of an associated Prince feel inappropriate.<br /> <br /> Instead, I could see the gameline represent the Broken Majesty's influence via mortal conspiracies, ranging from worshipful cults to secret societies trying to turn its own power against it, all making the situation worse by exploiting the Broken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-26T13:19:47-07:00","id":1391764,"title":"","content":"Sin-Eaters are immune from being claimed, but there's nothing that says they couldn't have been altered previous to their Bargain. Honestly with Sin-Eaters, I thought due to their relative rarity it might make more sense to just go straight ghosts instead, with the Broken Majesty making a twisted ghost, perhaps turned into an old-school geist that was part-ghost and part-spirit, but even then the idea kept merging with Sin-Eaters. So one of the interesting things the Gurdilag did was merge weird supernatural life forms in experimental methods. One of the interesting results, to me, was a werewolf that had been merged with an azlu.<br /> <br /> On one hand there's the idea of a Sin-Eater whose geist or human side or both have been merged with that of one of the hosts. This can lead to a dynamic that tears itself in opposite directions (especially if the two hosts are antagonistic, like beshilu or azlu), or something more like the Merovech or something that might start pulling the underworld and physical world closer together to the point that, in Bangkok subways and underground tunnels they might have completely overlapped.<br /> <br /> Another way to go might be for the Broken Majesty to, if it wants a vassal, usurp an existing ruler. Sweeping up and shifting around an entire Dead Domain. Then luring it out of its madness with the Bargain Numen and the right host, eventually leaving some poor once-dead sucker with an entire kingdom in his soul, the loudest voice being the tyrant king that used to rule.<br /> <br /> Similarly with Demons, it's easier for me to imagine a co-opting of Angels and infrastructure than getting much out of actual individual Demons. This could lead to squabbles in the local demon community, tearing them between seeing it as a good thing, or another worse thing.<br /> <br /> Also it's just basic google but all the results for colors in Thailand suggested some beliefs in lucky and unlucky colors associated with the days of the week, that might be linked to Buddhism. If the results are valid it might be a thing to base the colors scheme off of. Though I like the idea of an Unseen Prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}